WEBVTT

00:00:04.712 --> 00:00:09.587
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Fascinating facts about sugar and salt

00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:16.434
At different times in history, both sugar and salt were called “white gold”

00:00:16.627 --> 00:00:20.484
because they were so expensive and difficult to get.

00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:25.611
And there are many more interesting facts about sugar and salt…

00:00:28.622 --> 00:00:33.844
Salt is used to make glass, laundry detergent, and paper.

00:00:36.819 --> 00:00:43.943
People often think that sugar makes children more active or that it makes them behave badly.

00:00:44.463 --> 00:00:49.093
However, there is no strong scientific evidence of this.

00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:55.496
Salt was very valuable in ancient Rome.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.464
Soldiers were paid extra money called “salarium” especially to buy it, and

00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:05.019
this is where the word “salary” comes from.

00:01:08.061 --> 00:01:11.651
Scientists use sugar to make different kinds of plastic,

00:01:11.944 --> 00:01:14.227
for example, for food packaging.

00:01:17.221 --> 00:01:22.514
Only 4% of the salt used in the US is used in food;

00:01:23.068 --> 00:01:29.286
the remaining 96% is used for things like farming and de-icing roads.

00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:37.496
<i>Sure</i> and <i>sugar</i> are the only two words in the English language

00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:41.653
that begin with “su” and are pronounced “sh”.

00:01:44.964 --> 00:01:49.719
In the UK, there’s a club for people who collect the little packets of

00:01:49.744 --> 00:01:54.635
sugar you get when you order tea or coffee in a café or restaurant.

00:01:57.865 --> 00:02:04.112
Salt removes coffee stains (though probably not from your new white carpet).

00:02:07.266 --> 00:02:12.304
If you put sugar into a vase of flowers, the flowers last longer.

00:02:15.493 --> 00:02:20.932
The body of an average adult has about 250 g of salt.

00:02:21.521 --> 00:02:25.933
It helps oxygen travel around the body and makes muscles work.

00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:35.453
Salzburg, the city in Austria where Mozart was born, means “castle of salt.”

00:02:38.765 --> 00:02:45.900
Christopher Columbus introduced sugar to the Americas in 1493, on his second voyage.